---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const lastUpdated = 'October 4, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Benaya Tech"
  description="The terms that apply to the use of the Benaya Tech website and to smart-home, Wi-Fi, security, and installation work requested through it."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Terms & Conditions"
    sub={`The terms that apply to this website and to work requested through it. Last updated ${lastUpdated}.`}
  />

  <section class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl article-content">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of this website and any request you submit to {site.name}{' '}
        (“we,” “us,” or “our”). By using the site or submitting a request, you agree to them.
        Nothing in these terms limits rights you may have under applicable consumer protection law.
      </p>

      <h2>Our services</h2>
      <p>
        We design, install, configure, test, document, and support smart-home, Wi-Fi and
        networking, security camera, and technology installation projects for homes and small
        businesses in Northern Virginia. Information on this site is general in nature. It is not a
        quote, a guarantee of results, or technical advice for a specific property.
      </p>

      <h2>Requests, estimates, and scheduling</h2>
      <p>
        Submitting the request form does not create a contract and does not reserve an appointment.
        It begins a conversation. Work proceeds only once both parties have agreed in writing to a
        specific scope, through an estimate, proposal, or work order.
      </p>
      <p>
        Estimates are based on the information available when they are prepared and may be revised
        after an on-site assessment or if conditions differ from what was described. Where a written
        estimate, proposal, or invoice addresses scope, pricing, payment, scheduling, cancellation,
        or warranty, that document governs and takes precedence over this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide accurate information about the property and what you want to accomplish</li>
        <li>Provide safe, lawful access to the property and work areas on the scheduled date</li>
        <li>
          Obtain any permission required before work begins, including from a landlord, building
          owner, or homeowners association
        </li>
        <li>Ensure an authorized adult is available where access or decisions are required</li>
        <li>Keep your own account credentials, passwords, and access codes secure</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Existing wiring, network conditions, construction materials, and third-party equipment can
        affect what is achievable at a given property. We will tell you when we find such a
        constraint and discuss the options before proceeding.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party products and services</h2>
      <p>
        Equipment we install is manufactured by third parties and is covered by their warranties and
        terms, not ours. Some devices depend on services outside our control, such as your internet
        connection, a manufacturer's cloud platform, or a paid subscription. We are not responsible
        for third-party outages, account changes, pricing changes, feature removals, or decisions to
        discontinue a product or service.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment terms, deposits, and accepted methods are set out in your written estimate or
        invoice.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancellation and rescheduling</h2>
      <p>
        If you need to cancel or reschedule, contact us as early as you reasonably can so the
        appointment can be reassigned. Any notice requirements or charges that apply will be stated
        in your written estimate.
      </p>

      <h2>Workmanship</h2>
      <p>
        We perform work in a professional and workmanlike manner. Any warranty on our labor is
        stated in your written estimate or invoice. Except as stated there and as required by law,
        we make no other warranties regarding the work.
      </p>

      <h2>Website content</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this site, including text, layout, graphics, and the {site.name} name and
        logo, belongs to us or our licensors. You may view and share it for personal,
        non-commercial purposes. You may not copy, republish, or use it commercially without our
        written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You agree not to misuse this site: no attempts to disrupt or gain unauthorized access to it,
        no automated scraping or bulk collection of its content, and no submission of false requests
        or another person's details without their permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. We do not warrant that it
        will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that its content is complete or current at all times.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
        or consequential damages arising from your use of this site. For any claim arising from work
        we performed, our total liability is limited to the amount you paid us for that work.
        Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        This site may link to third-party websites. We do not control them and are not responsible
        for their content, products, or privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href={`${base}/privacy`}>Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle the information
        you share with us.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Virginia, without regard to its
        conflict of laws rules. Any dispute will be brought in the state or federal courts located
        in Virginia.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The current version will always be posted here with the date it
        was last updated. The terms in effect when you submitted your request apply to that request.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}<br />
        Email: <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a><br />
        Serving Northern Virginia
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
